{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDExLS0yMDE1L0x1bGxhYnklMjAlMjgyMDE0JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Lullaby","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/ghKDvp24lXKo6b1TtILweFKy6yV.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/1xFjrbb12NoGvXkdNt6KTiePpXX.jpg","description":"Estranged from his family, Jonathan (Hedlund) discovers his father has decided to take himself off life support in forty-eight hours’ time. During this intensely condensed period, a lifetime of drama plays out. Robert (Jenkins) fights a zero sum game to reclaim all that his illness stole from his family. A debate rages on patients’ rights and what it truly means to be free. Jonathan reconciles with his father, reconnects with his mother (Archer), sister (Brown-Findlay), and his love (Adams) and reclaims his voice through two unlikely catalysts – a young, wise-beyond-her-years patient (Barden) and a no-nonsense nurse (Hudson). Through this intensely life affirming prism, an unexpected and powerful journey of love, laughter, and forgiveness unfolds.\n\nReleased 13 Jun 2014 · United States of America · Language: English · 117 min\nStudio: Avenue Picture, Metalwork Pictures\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2014","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.2","runtime":"117 min","cast":["Garrett Hedlund","Richard Jenkins","Anne Archer","Jessica Brown Findlay","Amy Adams","Jessica Barden","Terrence Howard","Jennifer Hudson"],"director":["Andrew Levitas"],"released":"2014-06-13T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"What do you say when everything has been left unsaid?","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Andrew Levitas","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/15YMsSqttwT75cKQ9eiDPqfxjmh.jpg"},{"name":"Garrett Hedlund","character":"Jonathan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/9zec61HuFJgiUEzPSt0NfPIj0Xv.jpg"},{"name":"Richard Jenkins","character":"Robert","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/muT3RZG9hiKaKojD751RcQ5tG